---
// Dojo Tutor case study — DRAFT. Served at /dojo-tutor in local preview only
// (see src/pages/[draft].astro); it is not part of the live site.
// To publish: move this file to src/pages/dojo-tutor.astro (imports work as-is), remove
// it from src/pages/[draft].astro, remove `noindex`, and drop `draft: true` in src/data/site.ts.
// Image slots without a `name` render as placeholders: once a file is in
// src/assets/media (see README → Images), add `name: 'file-name'`.
import CaseStudy from '../layouts/CaseStudy.astro';
import Figure from '../components/Figure.astro';
---

<CaseStudy
  name="Dojo Tutor"
  tagline="is ClassDojo’s marketplace connecting tutors and families across a wide range of subjects, in both 1-on-1 and group formats."
  noindex
  details={[
    { label: 'Responsibilities', items: ['Product design', 'User research'] },
    { label: 'Collaborators', items: ['1 product manager', '1 product designer', '8 engineers'] },
    { label: 'Platforms', items: ['Web', 'iOS', 'Android'] },
    { label: 'Years', items: ['2024–Present'] },
  ]}
>
  <Fragment slot="meta">
    <p class="callout">
      Designed and shipped more than 75% of Dojo Tutor’s current product experience, often building features myself
      with AI coding agents. Grew M3 retention 12% and LTV 20% YoY.
    </p>
  </Fragment>

  <div class="intro">
    <p>
      I own the core product experience on both sides of the marketplace, from discovery and design through
      implementation, partnering closely with engineers and often shipping features myself.
    </p>
  </div>

  <Figure images={[{ alt: 'Hero image' }]} eager />

  <div class="section-head">
    <h2>Turning Dojo Tutor into a true marketplace and growing LTV by 20% YoY</h2>
    <p>
      Dojo Tutor launched in 2023 as a matching service: the platform paired students with tutors and charged a fixed
      price for all classes. The product was an MVP, but the goal was a true marketplace where tutors could grow and run
      their own businesses.
    </p>
    <p>
      Since joining in 2024, I’ve redesigned every post-purchase surface for tutors and families. I’ve also added the
      core features a marketplace needs: schedule management, tutor-set pricing, direct messaging, automated marketing
      tools, and payment management. For these, I used AI coding agents to build 70% of the parent surface frontends and
      80% of the tutor surface frontends, with backend contributions as well.
    </p>
  </div>

  <Figure
    images={[
      {
        alt: 'Dashboards, direct messaging, schedule management, insights, notification settings, payment history, and more',
      },
    ]}
  />

  <div class="section-head">
    <h2>Expanding from 1-on-1 tutoring to group classes and growing revenue by 10%</h2>
    <p>
      Dojo Tutor launched with 1-on-1 online tutoring only. In early 2026, we introduced group classes, our largest
      product expansion to date.
    </p>
    <p>
      I designed the tutor experience for creating and managing group classes, along with the internal tools our team
      uses to review class submissions.
    </p>
    <p>
      Within the first 8 months of launch, group classes accounted for 10% of Dojo Tutor’s revenue and are a strong
      contributor to overall revenue growth.
    </p>
  </div>

  <Figure images={[{ alt: 'Group class form' }, { alt: 'Group class dashboard' }]} />

  <div class="section-head">
    <h2>Letting tutors set their own prices</h2>
    <p>
      Prices used to be fixed by the platform. Dojo Tutor sought to allow tutors to set their own prices, allowing them to
      charge more for specialty topics as well as open up more affordable tutoring options for families. I designed and
      built much of the frontend for tutor pricing, including the first-time experience, setting rates, adding
      discounts, and surfacing market data so tutors can price competitively.
    </p>
    <p>Despite widespread apprehension from our tutor community, over 70% of tutors have opted into the new pricing model.</p>
  </div>

  <Figure images={[{ alt: 'Pricing onboarding' }, { alt: 'Setting prices screens' }]} />

  <div class="section-head">
    <h2>Launching iOS and Android apps for tutors</h2>
    <p>
      I designed native apps that let tutors message families, manage their classes, and claim open spots in classes
      that need a substitute. The app is slated to launch December 2026.
    </p>
  </div>

  <Figure images={[{ alt: 'Tutor app' }]} />
</CaseStudy>
